SWEET per-swap GPU witnesses (patch 0222, T-42ce, LOG ONLY: no register access, no behaviour change; boot-arg sweetpace=1 as patch 0186): the SWEET SWAPT line gains `busy_us W wait_us W call1 NS calll NS done NS` = GPU job busy time and submit-blocked time summed since the previous swap, the entry time of the first and of the latest sweet_mali_submit call and of the latest completion seen (uptime ns, 0 = none; call1 0 = no job since the previous swap). Separates "late start" (call1 far after the previous swap or the vsync) from "long render" (busy_us, done - call1) for the 20-33 ms swap-gap tail (docs/reviews/T-23cb-proof.md; CA a3 is only the display time, docs/research/T-42ce-ca-vsync-callback-a3.md). Lock-free reads as sweet_mali_seq_peek; values can be one job stale. Code: bsd/dev/sweet_mali.c, bsd/dev/sweet_mali.h, iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp. Needs patches 0145, 0186, 0212.
